  "description": "Shared CT01/CT04 vectors from contract.rs. repeat expands before real wire serialization; revisions always stay strings. Exactly one vector may confirm. This fixture carries no authority.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "32 vectors cover eight supplier fields, NFC and non-BMP Unicode, normalized/raw-name and text/list boundaries, allowed/invalid ratings, unsupported merged_into, unknown payload fields, and canonical decimal revisions.",
    "u64::MAX parses losslessly but existing command validation refuses mutation because no next revision exists; this case must return InvalidRevision during prepare. u64::MAX-1 and 2^53+1 use update proposals and must roundtrip as exact text.",
    "Only unicode-eight-fields confirms once through the real Service. Other valid proposals are discarded; invalid inputs must return exact errors and no plan. The committed eight-field value and original receipt must survive sole-client Service close/reopen with a new epoch.",
    "Not a complete malformed-JSON or UTF-16-fuzz corpus: duplicate keys, isolated surrogates, every optional-field raw UTF-16 limit, concurrent revocation, and model/provider metadata authority are outside these additional vectors. Existing dedicated contract and lifecycle tests retain those separate responsibilities."
